test.yaml:1:1: workflow has no "concurrency:", so a run that a schedule or a person starts executes at the same time as a run that is still going. add a top-level "concurrency:" with a "group:" such as "${{ github.workflow }}", so that a new run waits for the running one. do not add "cancel-in-progress: true" unless a run can be thrown away without losing work: nothing supersedes such a run, so a cancelled one is not started again. a run that is waiting is replaced by a newer one that is waiting, so for a manual run that takes inputs add them to the group, or add "queue: max" when no run may be skipped [concurrency-limits]
